<header>
    <p class="fc-eyebrow">Website administrator guide · Technical reference</p>
    <h1>The EmailManagement app</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">How an email gets from the website to someone's inbox: the hand-over, the email app's API, its queue and send loop, templates, delivery tracking and authentication.</p>
    <div class="docs-meta"><span>Repo: <code>shotgn16/EmailManagement-ForestChurches</code>, branch <code>feature/delivery-status</code></span><span>URL: <code>https://api.forestchurches.co.uk</code></span></div>
</header>

<h2>Why a separate app</h2>
<p>The website never talks to a mail server. Every email is handed to <strong>EmailManagement</strong>, a small ASP.NET Core 8 Web API hosted on a Plesk server, which holds the SMTP credentials, fills in the HTML template, and sends in batches. This keeps SMTP details out of the web app and lets the website respond immediately.</p>

