</div>
<p>To change an email's wording or design, edit the template in the <strong>EmailManagement</strong> repo and redeploy it. To change which values are passed, edit the matching <code>MailSender</code> method in ForestChurches. Placeholder names in the template and in <code>Data</code> must match exactly, including the braces.</p>

<h2>API reference</h2>
<div class="docs-table-wrap">
    <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Response</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>POST /Email</code></td><td>JWT</td><td>Queue an email.</td><td><code>{ id, status, receivedUtc, queueLength }</code>; 400 if no recipient.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>POST /Email/send</code></td><td>JWT</td><td>Send everything in the queue (used internally).</td><td><code>{ sent, retrying, failed, queueLength }</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>GET /Email/{id}/status</code></td><td>JWT</td><td>Status of one email.</td><td><code>{ id, status, attempts, receivedUtc, lastAttemptUtc, sentUtc, error }</code>; 404 with <code>status: "Unknown"</code> if not known.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>GET /Email/health</code></td><td>JWT</td><td>Is the app up, and how busy is it?</td><td>Includes <code>lastSendRunUtc</code>, <code>queueLength</code> and counts per status (queued, sent, failed…).</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>/swagger</code></td><td>None</td><td>Interactive API documentation (enabled in production by <code>EnableSwaggerInProduction: true</code>).</td><td>HTML</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>Statuses in the email app: <code>Queued</code> → <code>Sending</code> → <code>Sent</code>, or <code>Retrying</code> → … → <code>Failed</code>.</p>

<h2>Authentication between the apps</h2>
<p>The email app accepts a request only with a valid JWT: signature (HMAC-SHA256), issuer <code>ForestChurches</code>, audience <code>F0rest_Ch3rches</code> and lifetime are all checked.</p>
<div class="docs-callout docs-callout--danger">
    <span class="docs-callout__title">The email app's signing key is hard-coded</span>
    <p>In <code>EmailManagement/Program.cs</code> the issuer, audience <strong>and signing key</strong> used to <em>validate</em> tokens are written into the code, not read from Key Vault. For the two apps to work together, the Key Vault secret <code>jwt-token-securityKey</code> (and <code>jwt-token-issuer</code> / <code>jwt-token-audience</code>) must hold exactly the same values. This means:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>anyone with read access to the EmailManagement repository can create valid tokens and send email as <em>info@forestchurches.co.uk</em> through the app;</li>
        <li>rotating the key needs a code change and redeploy of the email app <em>and</em> a Key Vault update, at the same time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Fix: read the validation key, issuer and audience from Key Vault in the email app as well (see <a asp-page="/Docs/Admin/Security" asp-fragment="rotating-secrets">Rotating secrets</a>).</p>
</div>

