<h2>Troubleshooting email</h2>
<div class="docs-table-wrap">
    <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Check / fix</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Email delivery shows <em>Not received</em> for everything; email app <em>Problem</em></td><td>Email app down, DNS/TLS problem, or JWT rejected (401).</td><td>Open <code>https://api.forestchurches.co.uk/swagger</code>. Check the error under the status: 401 means the Key Vault JWT secrets don't match the email app's hard-coded values.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><em>Waiting to send</em> for more than 10 minutes; "Last send run" is old</td><td>The send loop has stopped (for example Key Vault or <code>app-email-url</code> unreachable from Plesk).</td><td>Restart the email app on Plesk; check its log files.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><em>Couldn't send</em></td><td>SMTP sign-in failed, address rejected, or template missing.</td><td>Read the error. Check the SMTP secrets and that the template exists in the email app's <code>templates</code> folder.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><em>No record</em></td><td>The email app restarted and lost its queue.</td><td>Those emails are lost; ask people to repeat the action.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><em>Sent</em> but not in the inbox</td><td>Spam filtering.</td><td>Ask the recipient to check spam; check SPF/DKIM/DMARC for forestchurches.co.uk at IONOS.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Link in email says expired</td><td>Token older than its lifetime, or Data Protection keys changed.</td><td>Send a new email. If every link fails, check the key ring in blob storage.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
